<section class="hot-chapter hot-wrap hot-narrow" id="questions"><p class="hot-eyebrow">Questions</p><h2>Before you order for New Year’s Eve</h2><div class="hot-faq" style="margin-top:20px"><details><summary>When should I order for New Year’s Eve?</summary><p class="hot-a">Orders ship Tuesday or Wednesday and usually arrive Wednesday or Thursday, and delivery is not guaranteed for an exact day. An order placed before 8am PT on Monday, December 21 ships Tuesday the 22nd; with your Christmas order is calmer still.</p></details><details><summary>How do I handle the caviar?</summary><p class="hot-a">Tins arrive frozen; keep them in the freezer until the day. Defrost in the refrigerator for about 5 hours, away from strongly scented foods. Do not refreeze after thawing, and finish an opened tin within 4 days.</p></details><details><summary>Can I host it as a sushi night?</summary><p class="hot-a">Yes. One steelhead loin and one pot of rice make five kinds of sushi, set out so everyone builds their own. <a href="/blogs/seatopia-collective-community/how-to-host-a-sushi-dinner-party-a-celebration-of-food-friends-amp-ritual">Our guide to hosting a sushi dinner party</a> has the rest.</p></details></div><p style="margin-top:16px"><a href="/pages/holiday-seafood-guide#before">More answers in the holiday guide</a></p></section>
